title: entry1
position: -365,-203
---
It seems like a war is coming again

The winds carry stories—  
Scattered whispers of the Demon King rising again.

We dismissed them at first.  
Tales spun by frightened traders and wandering monks.

But the forest's gone quiet.  
No birdsong. No breeze.  
Only the stillness of something watching.
->read
  <<jump entry2>>

===
title: entry2
position: -104,-201
---
It’s been two months since the second war started

A rider came through the night.  
No horse beneath him—just smoke and screaming hooves.  
He spoke of an army that bleeds sap instead of blood.

He said they do not march—they grow.  
Out of the ground.  
Out of our dead.

We haven’t seen them yet...  
But the roots near the graves are stirring.
->read
  <<jump entry3>>

===
title: entry3
position: 160,-205
---
They caught Rellen last night.  

Dragged him beneath the roots.  
His screams faded like breath in winter.

By morning, he was part of the forest.  
His ribs curled around a tree trunk.  
His eyes still wide, still begging.
->read
  <<jump entry4>>

===
title: entry4
position: 163,-45
---
They don’t eat us.  

They plant us.  
Bury us alive.  
Let the forest drink our decay.

Blood becomes sap.  
Bones become weapons.  
I held a spear made from someone’s spine.
->read
  <<jump entry5>>

===
title: entry5
position: 166,135
---
I ran.  
They let me.  
Laughed.

The trees laughed too.

They want me to carry this.  
To tell you.  
The woods are no longer woods.  

They’re hungry.
->read
  <<jump entry6>>

===
title: entry6
position: 165,349
---
If you find this...  
Don’t come looking.

Don’t bury us.  
Don’t pray for us.

Just burn it.  
Burn the forest until even the ashes scream.

-> END
